{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "dsh-web-on-another-port-is-not-this-port-server",
  "title": "dsh web on another port is not this port server",
  "requirement": "kit-update --check --json must answer two questions from one /proc scan: the profile's port is busy only when a dsh web declared that port (or answers HTTP there), and the pids offered to a restart are only that port's. Any dsh web on the machine still blocks a harness replacement, and the check's own process tree is never named.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "verified",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "scripts/test/kit-update-server-scope.test.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node --test scripts/test/kit-update-server-scope.test.mjs",
  "steps": [
    "Start a synthetic dsh web on a free port: node <tmp>/.../lib/bin.js web --port <foreign>.",
    "Run node scripts/kit-update.mjs --check --json --kit . --home <tmp home> --port <free port>.",
    "Run the same check with --port <foreign>.",
    "Start a synthetic dsh web whose command line is the check's own parent, and run the check beneath it with the same port.",
    "Call convergeHarness from the imported module with the machine-wide scan while a dsh web lives in another home on another port, and again with an empty machine."
  ],
  "expected": "A foreign-port process leaves server.running false with empty pids for the other port and makes it true only for its own port; the ancestor chain is absent while a non-ancestor server on the same port stays listed; convergeHarness blocks with reason web-server-running on the machine-wide scan and lets the replacement through when nothing runs.",
  "tags": [
    "kit-update",
    "server-watchdog",
    "proc-scan"
  ],
