  "failsWhen": "The /proc scan stops filtering by declared port (any dsh web makes the profile port look busy again), the check's own process tree is named as a server, or the harness gate starts reading the port-filtered list.",
  "trigger": "A dsh web server started with --port on a port other than the profile's, while kit-update --check --json runs with the profile's port.",
  "oracle": "The requirement: --port names one profile's port, so only that port's server may make it busy and only that port's pids may be stopped; the harness gate must stay machine-wide because a server of any port keeps its boot composition.",
